    "result_text": "The test passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change request \u2014 \"Show money properly everywhere. Use a dollar sign and cents, like $100.00\" \u2014 was a UI-display-only change (the spec confirms the audit format is unchanged: `amount=100.00`, and money values already flow through the app as numbers, so no schema or server change was needed).\n\n**What I did**, following the app's additive conventions:\n\n1. **New shared file** `ui/money.ts` \u2014 a single `money(amount)` formatter returning `` `$${amount.toFixed(2)}` `` (e.g. `$100.00`). This matches CLAUDE.md's rule that `ui/**` holds shared presentational primitives, composed rather than duplicated.\n\n2. **Removed the two duplicated local `money()` helpers** (in `InvoicesPanel.tsx` and `Dashboard.tsx`) and pointed both at the shared one. That covers every money surface \u2014 invoice rows (`invoice-amount`), the project total (`project-invoices-total`), and the dashboard outstanding total (`dashboard-outstanding-total`) \u2014 so money renders identically \"everywhere.\"\n\nNo `data-testid` values were renamed or removed. `bin/e2e` builds, starts, and passes the acceptance spec (`$100.00` per row, `$150.00` total).",
